<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Satsuma Domain</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Satsuma</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Satsuma Domain was a powerful feudal domain in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyushu">Kyushu</a>, ruled by the Shimazu family. During the late Tokugawa period it acquired Western weapons and military training. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-shogunate">Tokugawa Shogunate</a> profile notes that Satsuma, together with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/choshu-domain">Choshu</a>, led the opposition that overthrew the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogunate</a> and brought about the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meiji-restoration">Meiji Restoration</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/satsuma-domain.jpg" alt="Satsuma Domain" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mass Ave 975 at English Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kagoshimajo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
